# Adding a lint rule

Use `AnalysisRule` / `MultiAnalysisRule` + `registerNodeProcessors`. Report with `rule.reportAtNode(node, diagnosticCode: ...)`.
Do not use `custom_lint_builder` or `DartLintRule`.

## Prefer the existing rule

Architecture import checks belong in `NoScreensDependenciesRule` (`MultiAnalysisRule`) so each file still has one `ImportDirective` visitor. Add a `LintCodeArchitecture` in `lint_utils.dart` and include it in `diagnosticCodes`.

A new rule class is only justified when the check cannot share that visitor.

Reuse `isInLayer`, `importsFromLayer`, `resolveImport`.
Use the full file path (`context.currentUnit?.file.path`), not `shortName`.

## After changing diagnostics

1. `registry.registerLintRule(...)` and export from `lib/main.dart` if you added a class
2. Enable the diagnostic name in `example/analysis_options.yaml` under `plugins.clean_arch_lint.diagnostics`
3. Examples in `example/lib/{layer}/`
4. Tests for any new `import_resolver` behavior
5. Dartdoc on the rule / `LintCode` (severity, violation, yaml)
6. README.md, USAGE.md, RULES.md, CHANGELOG.md

```dart
@override
FutureOr<void> register(PluginRegistry registry) {
  registry.registerLintRule(NoScreensDependenciesRule());
}
```
